  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will continue around the south-western base for a\neastern CONUS trough. The pattern will bring a high probability\nof dry, seasonable weather (highs in 70s, lows in upper 40s/low\n50s) through at least next Tuesday. Chances of rain have gone\ndown even more in early week with shortwaves around the trough \ndisplaced east in more recent guidance.\n\nTemperature uncertainty increases mid-week with ensembles\nindecisive of ridging or the stagnation of a closed low around\nthe eastern seaboard. This may be the difference between\nremaining seasonable or temperatures trending ~10F above \naverage Wednesday/Thursday, but most likely dry in any scenario.\n\nNext Friday into Saturday, confidence increases in ridging\nwinning out, but there is more uncertainty in temperatures \naffiliated with a digging surface front late-week which will \nalso return the next sizable chance of any rain. CIPS also \nalludes this as the next non-zero chance of severe weather.",
